WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.800
"The Suicide Squad" is unlike any other&nbsp;
film the in the DCEU. It's gorier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.440
it's more chaotic, and it's hysterical. There's&nbsp;
also a lot that happens at the end. While the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.840
movie has a clear resolution, there are some&nbsp;
nuances worth examining in further detail.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.240
Let's dive in — with an obvious spoiler warning.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.280
After the Suicide Squad finally makes their way&nbsp;
to Jotunheim, they split up into two groups: one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.820
to track down the villainous starfish-like being&nbsp;
known as Starro, and another to plant explosives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:30.632
Rick Flagg leads the group bringing the Thinker to&nbsp;
Starro, where they find out several awful truths.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.632 --> 00:00:36.134
First, Starro spits out mini starfish which&nbsp;
latch on to hosts, murder them, and become an&nbsp;extension of Starro. &nbsp;

00:00:36.134 --> 00:00:39.520
Second, Starro came from&nbsp;
outer space -- a fact known to the audience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.440
but not to most of the characters. Third, and&nbsp;
most damningly, Starro was being researched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.634
on and kept in Corto Maltese at the behest of the&nbsp;
United States government for maximum deniability.

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:52.640
Meanwhile, the bomb planting squad, partially&nbsp;
led by Bloodsport, starts working their way up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.040
the tower and setting up explosives. A few&nbsp;
crucial miscommunications result in a bomb&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.520
being destroyed early, which sets off a chain&nbsp;
detonation and slowly levels the building.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.800
It's right around this time that Flagg&nbsp;
grabs a hard drive and declares he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.560
going to reveal the truth to the American&nbsp;
press -- only to find out that Peacemaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:13.020
had secret orders from Amanda Waller to make&nbsp;
sure that info never saw the light of day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:16.800
Everyone on the lower level gets knocked out&nbsp;
by the blast, and a struggle ensues between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.680
Flagg and Peacemaker over the hard drive -- one&nbsp;
which ends in Flagg's death. Peacemaker tries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.560
to kill Ratcatcher II, but Bloodsport manages to&nbsp;
survive the explosion and shoots Peacemaker first.

00:01:27.668 --> 00:01:31.760
Starro, now free and having killed the Thinker,&nbsp;
starts wreaking havoc on the nearby city. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:36.320
the hostile government destabilized, Waller&nbsp;
declares the mission complete -- but Bloodsport,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:42.000
Polka-Dot Man, Ratcatcher II, King Shark,&nbsp;
and Harley decide that they're not done until&nbsp;Starro is defeated. &nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.880
Waller comes inches from&nbsp;
detonating the bombs in their necks, but is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.680
knocked out by her own employees. Bloodsport&nbsp;
takes charge and organizes a plan of attack.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:53.200
After a grueling battle in which each&nbsp;
member uses their own special abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.800
Starro is defeated. Alas, Polka-Dot&nbsp;
Man dies during the battle.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:59.184
"We're all gonna die."
"I hope so."&nbsp;

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.440
At this time, the Corto Maltese freedom&nbsp;
fighters topple the military leadership and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.600
plan to establish a new democratic government.&nbsp;
By this point, the squad's exploits and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.000
death of Starro are worldwide news and seen&nbsp;
by Bloodsport's daughter half a world away.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.640
Bloodsport, who held onto the drive, uploads&nbsp;
it to a secure server, giving Waller a choice:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:21.120
their immediate freedom, or he'll release the&nbsp;
info. Waller acknowledges that Bloodsport did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.760
indeed become a leader and accepts his terms. Even&nbsp;
though America's involvement will be kept secret,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.588
the Squad gets their freedom&nbsp;
and saves a sovereign nation.&nbsp;

00:02:28.588 --> 00:02:31.760
Mid-and-post credit scenes reveal that&nbsp;
Weasel survived the beach assault and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.960
that Peacemaker barely survived, and&nbsp;
that there's a mission ready for him.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.560
Now that we've recapped the ending,&nbsp;
let's break down some of the themes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.400
and how the movie set them up. We'll start by&nbsp;
acknowledging what Waller promised at the start:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.840
that she'd make Bloodsport a leader.
Bloodsport spends the film showing bits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:51.000
and pieces of leadership. He and Flagg also do&nbsp;
most of the planning for their abortive rescue of Harley Quinn. &nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.560
Bloodsport also acts as the de&nbsp;
facto leader of the group at the top of the tower,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.600
taking point on the operation.
By the time Starro is up and kicking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.640
Rick Flagg is dead and Peacemaker&nbsp;
has betrayed the group - and is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:04.640
also seemingly dead himself. This is also&nbsp;
the moment Bloodsport becomes a leader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.080
and it happens so organically that he&nbsp;
doesn't even notice. He's the first member&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.080
to ignore Waller's orders and the one who gives&nbsp;
instructions on how they should fight Starro.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:16.947
If Bloodsport is the heart of Task Force X,&nbsp;
Ratcatcher II is the soul. &nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.947 --> 00:03:20.880
While summoning the rat army, she remembers her late&nbsp;
father. In one of the most tear-jerking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:24.480
moments of the whole film, Ratcatcher&nbsp;
tells his daughter why he loves rats:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.480
because if these vile creatures can find a&nbsp;
place for themselves in the world, anyone can.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:34.080
The surviving members of Task Force X are largely&nbsp;
morally decent or at least morally neutral people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:39.200
driven to crime by circumstance. Bloodsport is&nbsp;
a mercenary, King Shark is a creature of pure id&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.920
too stupid to be good or evil, Polka-Dot Man was&nbsp;
the victim of an experiment, and Ratcatcher II was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:48.960
left alone after her father tragically died and&nbsp;
all she had were the rats. Indeed, Ratcatcher II's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:53.680
rat identified Bloodsport as a good person early&nbsp;
on, and she reminds Bloodsport of that later.&nbsp;

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:57.920
More than anything, however, they're misfits.&nbsp;
None of them quite gelled with the outside word,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:01.840
with Bloodsport, who is still a&nbsp;
neglectful father, the closest to normal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:07.280
King Shark never had a friend before Ratcatcher II&nbsp;
offered to become his. Polka-Dot Man is a tragic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:11.920
lonely, figure whose shyness is compounded&nbsp;
by a deeply embarrassing power. Harley has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:16.320
thrice been unlucky in love and has struggled&nbsp;
to find her place after breaking up with Joker.&nbsp;

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:19.030
It's unknown what each will do with their newfound&nbsp;
freedom. &nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:22.868
But like rats, these vile creatures have found a place for themselves in the world.

